]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-04T22:02:42-08:00","id":1475824,"title":"","content":"Wait what? Is this in concept the same Player's Guide that Mophidius was developing before getting booted off the property? They're still trying to do it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-05T03:20:36-08:00","id":1475829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475813-player-s-guide-and-blood-sigils-for-vtm-announced?p=1475824#post1475824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait what? Is this in concept the same Player's Guide that Mophidius was developing before getting booted off the property? They're still trying to do it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean it was half-done. Hence why the Vampire: The Masquerade Companion exists.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-05T04:55:11-08:00","id":1475834,"title":"","content":"i couldn't find any announcements. Do we have the links for them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/22488-ventruestereotype","name":"VentrueStereotype","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-05T05:35:36-08:00","id":1475836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VentrueStereotype</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475813-player-s-guide-and-blood-sigils-for-vtm-announced?p=1475834#post1475834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i couldn't find any announcements. Do we have the links for them?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It was in the RenegadeCon stream yesterday, and Outstar said on discord they'll have announcement pages next week.<br /> <br /> Here's a longer breakdown of the four Vampire announcements.<ul><li>Vampire Player's Guide due summer 2022, with all the non-core clans in one spot, updates to the Companion material, alternate banes, character creation walkthrough and other mechanics.</li> <li>Vampire Character Journal, an organized journal for all of your character stuff, allies, relationship map, etc.</li> <li>Vampire Starter Set, box set w/all tools to learn how to play or to teach people how to play VtM or update old players to V5. Come w/pregens, quickstart rules and story.</li> <li>Blood Sigils, a Blood Sorcery and Thin Blood Alchemy book, will not only have BS and Alchemy mechanics but also stuff for the Blood Sorcery scene in general, providing locations, component information, and other source material that will give you Story Hooks for your game</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-05T12:40:58-08:00","id":1475854,"title":"","content":"There's a thaumaturgy companion after they nuked thaumaturgy? Will this be backtracking or will they go all in on nu &quot;Blood Sorcery&quot;/TBA?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-05T22:05:45-08:00","id":1475878,"title":"","content":"Alternative banes? I might get back into v5 then. Unless the players guide is as expensive as the Sabbat book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T01:27:39-08:00","id":1475884,"title":"","content":"The blood sorcery book inflation is happening faster than I expected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-07T10:33:11-08:00","id":1475989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475813-player-s-guide-and-blood-sigils-for-vtm-announced?p=1475829#post1475829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean it was half-done. Hence why the Vampire: The Masquerade Companion exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but I figured that when the Companion released, that that was that. I didn\u2019t think they\u2019d try again to get it released.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-07T16:30:37-08:00","id":1476006,"title":"","content":"The Lasombra are the only ones who really need an alternate bane. The rest are fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-07T17:41:05-08:00","id":1476011,"title":"","content":"They also sideways-announced **Hot Summer Nights** which is apparently a Miami sourcebook for V5. I couldn't find anything that they actually talked about it other than it's a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-08T02:58:25-08:00","id":1476036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475813-player-s-guide-and-blood-sigils-for-vtm-announced?p=1475989#post1475989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, but I figured that when the Companion released, that that was that. I didn\u2019t think they\u2019d try again to get it released.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looks like they're trying to make everything to date available in print and in shops. So it makes sense. E.g., they have redone the screen and Book of Nod, and are making retail versions of CbN and CotBG.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-08T03:00:53-08:00","id":1476037,"title":"","content":"This could be interesting, one way or another.<br /> Alternate banes sounds good. The Assamites, Salubri and Hecata immediately jump to mind, since those are the clans comprised of bloodlines with different weaknesses. In the case of the latter, Giovanni embraces were occasionally known to result in Cappadocians anyway, so.<br /> (Alternate discipline spreads, as in Cult of the Blood Gods, wouldn't be a bad idea either).<br /> <br /> I won't ever care about Alchemy, but I am very curious about the Blood Sorcery and whether I'm going to regard it as an improvement or not. Is it going to explore the various paradigms and flesh them out rather than presenting a vague mishmash of Thaumaturgy and Quietus/Dur-An-Ki? Is there Koldunic Sorcery? Technomancy? It seems like kind of an important tool for the 21st century, no?? Anarch sorcerers? Is Akhu blood sorcery, oblivion or an amalgam of both? Will Abyss Mysticism and Necromancy get any focus, or is there meant to be an Oblivion supplement?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-08T04:20:30-08:00","id":1476038,"title":"","content":"I really hope we get a nice comprehensive player guide, there's been a bit of a dirth of player content after the last of the Onyx Path books got published. (I'd love to see more content by them too.) Some new clan merits (a la Lore of the Clans/Bloodlines) and loresheets wouldn't go amiss. I think some re-works to the clan banes would also be great, the Lasombra and Salubri especially could do with a new set in my opinion, maybe some options for the Hecata Bloodlines (just to help depict older characters, personally don't mind the amalgamation that much).<br /> <br /> I'm rather surprised we're already getting a new Blood-Sorcery and Alchemy book. I was under the impression-V5 was intended to move away from that older style of design. Then again, reintroducing some versatility won't hurt, so long as we don't wind-up with V20 thaumaturgy, etc. Could be good to see Thin-Blood Alchemy given another look-in as well, make into something a bit more useful for a coterie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STV Author - <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/374164/Guide-to-the-Sabbat?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=0_0_45624_0_0_0_0\" target=\"_blank\">Guide to the Sabbat</a> <br /> Current Project(s): Tales from the Fronts - A Guide to the Gehenna War","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25061-karos","name":"Karos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25061_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-08T04:47:39-08:00","id":1476039,"title":"","content":"A thin blood alchemy book makes sense. V5 is weirdly focussed on them as a player option (occasionally to its detriment) but as presented alchemy stinks so this is going to be very useful for their 'vision' moving forward.<br /> <br /> It'd be nice to get some more blood sorcery powers which establish more meaningful distinctions between tremere and assamite blood magic. It would also be good to implement some powers that feel more like magic as opposed to corebook were its presented as just a vitae manipulation power line up with some rituals stapled on.<br /> <br /> It's a very very good thing that they're releasing a players guide with the other clans. Needing 4 supplementary books to play 20+ year old player options was outright embarissing for the company. Especially when compared to revised or v20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 03-09-2022, 08:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-08T09:08:20-08:00","id":1476049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475813-player-s-guide-and-blood-sigils-for-vtm-announced?p=1476036#post1476036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Looks like they're trying to make everything to date available in print and in shops. So it makes sense. E.g., they have redone the screen and Book of Nod, and are making retail versions of CbN and CotBG.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're also releasing the various stretch goal books in print as well, preorders are already up for a few of then on Renegade's site. Seeing as a stated goal was for V5 to maintain a presence in stores, at least they're pushing forward with that with Renegade.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475813-player-s-guide-and-blood-sigils-for-vtm-announced?p=1476038#post1476038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm rather surprised we're already getting a new Blood-Sorcery and Alchemy book. I was under the impression-V5 was intended to move away from that older style of design. Then again, reintroducing some versatility won't hurt, so long as we don't wind-up with V20 thaumaturgy, etc. Could be good to see Thin-Blood Alchemy given another look-in as well, make into something a bit more useful for a coterie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dots sell books. I wouldn't expect to see anything along the lines of old Thaumaturgy though, with Paths and such; every release since the core has kept the standard mandate of 'Blood Sorcery is things that manipulate the blood in some way, and rituals are magic effects brought about by the use of blood as a ritual catalyst'. We'll see more things along the lines of of how fire summoning became in the Chicago books, and such like that. Hopefully they are able to keep stuff from being written that steps on other Disciplines' niches, which is my bigger concern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1808,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","user":"elmerg","date":". 03-08-2022, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-08T10:28:20-08:00","id":1476053,"title":"","content":"I really don't like the whole &quot;Vampire sorcery is BLOOD sorcery&quot; because it misses out on the whole idea of Thaumaturgy as an enlightenment/self betterment practice that's available to everyone. And, also, it's kinda juvenile. As someone here excellently put it (I can't remember who, sorry) it'd be silly if werewolves where only using wolfy wolf magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-08T10:46:48-08:00","id":1476055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475813-player-s-guide-and-blood-sigils-for-vtm-announced?p=1476053#post1476053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't like the whole &quot;Vampire sorcery is BLOOD sorcery&quot; because it misses out on the whole idea of Thaumaturgy as an enlightenment/self betterment practice that's available to everyone. And, also, it's kinda juvenile. As someone here excellently put it (I can't remember who, sorry) it'd be silly if werewolves where only using wolfy wolf magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dislike it for a different reason: vampires in fiction rarely manipulate blood directly. By in large, vampires control the weather, cause doors to open and close, and cause candles to light. When vampires are wizard-like in fiction, they basically have weather-thaum, movement of the mind, and lure of flames.<br /> <br /> Personally I'd be fine if they replaced movement of the mind and lure of flames with some kind of ritual you could cast on your home that gave you limited control over it, allowing you to have a specialized version of MOTM and LOF without its broader applications, but just booting both powers entirely feels wrong.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-08T12:36:02-08:00","id":1476058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475813-player-s-guide-and-blood-sigils-for-vtm-announced?p=1476053#post1476053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't like the whole &quot;Vampire sorcery is BLOOD sorcery&quot; because it misses out on the whole idea of Thaumaturgy as an enlightenment/self betterment practice that's available to everyone. And, also, it's kinda juvenile. As someone here excellently put it (I can't remember who, sorry) it'd be silly if werewolves where only using wolfy wolf magic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I mean it makes about much sense as all the werewolf theurge powers having wolf motifs....or people motifs if you're a lupus. All you're energy attacks firing glowing bits of people everywhere. <br /> <br /> Taking this idea further you'd have the order of Hermes firing loafs of bread at everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-08T15:42:05-08:00","id":1476065,"title":"","content":"I think Vampire magic should have some general rule for it with interchangeable catalysts for distinct groups/styles. That said, I really don't mind the theme of blood <b>for the Tremere</b>, as it plays well on their specific history: alchemists (not only, but greatly) that became vampires by the power of a blood-based concoction and lost their previous magic in the process, now examining the power of the Blood as a substitute.<br /> <br /> But while I think versatility in execution, at least from an OoC perspective, would work nice, mechanically I don't miss old sorcery either.<br /> <br /> On the matter that dots sell books, if they want to keep churning books at a steady pace that'll be entirely true, and magic is always a good vector to do this. Heck, even Mage managed to do this with a core system that made every new spell redundant by definition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-08T19:50:26-08:00","id":1476075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475813-player-s-guide-and-blood-sigils-for-vtm-announced?p=1476011#post1476011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They also sideways-announced **Hot Summer Nights** which is apparently a Miami sourcebook for V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where did you hear about this?<br /> <br /> Because it sounds more like a fan book over on the Vault than an official book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 03-08-2022, 10:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-09T00:03:25-08:00","id":1476083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475813-player-s-guide-and-blood-sigils-for-vtm-announced?p=1476075#post1476075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because it sounds more like a fan book over on the Vault than an official book.</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds more like an old Miami-based action or police series than a Vampire book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-09T09:31:14-08:00","id":1476098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475813-player-s-guide-and-blood-sigils-for-vtm-announced?p=1476075#post1476075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where did you hear about this?<br /> <br /> Because it sounds more like a fan book over on the Vault than an official book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It was mentioned by Renegade staff in the Storyteller's panel that happened on Saturday. It wasn't a formal announcement of the book, apparently, but it was mentioned as a thing happening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-09T10:06:57-08:00","id":1476102,"title":"","content":"The Old Thaumaturgy gave the theological ideas of Noddists, the Baharri, Tremere, Followers of Set and Assamites some legitimacy. Now they have a few vulgar and bloody magic tricks with nothing noble beyond that, as if they're pedalling a scam. A lot of wind has been taken out of these sails. Even if you're not playing a thaumaturge, it's a heavy blow to the setting. The writer is welcome to think all cults are evil, but it's another thing to rewrite them from flawed faiths into bad jokes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-09T18:50:22-08:00","id":1476135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475813-player-s-guide-and-blood-sigils-for-vtm-announced#post1475813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blood Sigils is a Blood Sorcery and Thin blood Alchemy sourcebook</div> </div> </div> </div>The book on Miami is a bit of a surprise, but <i>Blood Sigils</i> makes sense as something to be released in the near future. Most of the books produced with the CotBG Kickstarter have been released, and so has the Sabbat book. The SI book is also coming. So that covers a new location, a bunch of vampire social clubs, the Sabbat, the big mortal antagonist group, and all the clans are presented by now and will be collected in a single book. A book on blood magic will mean most of the major areas will be covered. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-09T22:39:36-08:00","id":1476150,"title":"","content":"Hopefully, we will get some &quot;Descendants Of&quot; loresheets for some clans who don't have it yet such as the Banu Haqim, Ministry, Tzimisce, Ravnos, and the Salubri.<br /> <br /> For the blood sorcery book, wish we get some info on Kolduns (possibly even the Revenants) and even a bloodlines loresheet.<br /> <br /> for the &quot;Descendants Of&quot; loresheets, here is what I hope for<br /> <br /> Tzimisce: Dracon, Dracula, Kartarirya, Ruthven<br /> <br /> Banu Haqim: Ur Shulgi, Mancheaka<br /> <br /> Ministry: Keminitri, Damballah<br /> <br /> Ravnos: Hajimel, Ravana.<br /> <br /> Salubri: Rayzeel, Samiel, The Wu Zao Twins.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25313-raziel","name":"Raziel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-10T10:42:07-08:00","id":1476164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raziel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475813-player-s-guide-and-blood-sigils-for-vtm-announced?p=1476150#post1476150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hopefully, we will get some &quot;Descendants Of&quot; loresheets for some clans who don't have it yet such as the Banu Haqim, Ministry, Tzimisce, Ravnos, and the Salubri.<br /> <br /> For the blood sorcery book, wish we get some info on Kolduns (possibly even the Revenants) and even a bloodlines loresheet.<br /> <br /> for the &quot;Descendants Of&quot; loresheets, here is what I hope for<br /> <br /> Tzimisce: Dracon, Dracula, Kartarirya, Ruthven<br /> <br /> Banu Haqim: Ur Shulgi, Mancheaka<br /> <br /> Ministry: Keminitri, Damballah<br /> <br /> Ravnos: Hajimel, Ravana.<br /> <br /> Salubri: Rayzeel, Samiel, The Wu Zao Twins.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if Ur Shulgi has descendants, and I wouldn't personally be interested in them, either.<br /> <br /> For the Salubri, with how much Saulot himself was active during Revised, it could be interesting to have some new lineages coming from recent Embraces. He's the kind to do this kind of experiment, and reaching from 4th to 13th Generation doesn't have to take that long if you really decide you want to (One year is plenty of time to have your childe capable enough to Embrace if you're giving no fucks to Traditions or Princes, we had more than 20 years since Saulot interacting with PCs in Lair of the Hidden).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-10T14:19:09-08:00","id":1476170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475813-player-s-guide-and-blood-sigils-for-vtm-announced?p=1476164#post1476164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure if Ur Shulgi has descendants, and I wouldn't personally be interested in them, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Supposedly something like 2/3 of all Assamite sorcerers are descended from him, most prominently Al-Ashrad.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-10T17:10:19-08:00","id":1476177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475813-player-s-guide-and-blood-sigils-for-vtm-announced?p=1476164#post1476164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure if Ur Shulgi has descendants, and I wouldn't personally be interested in them, either.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ur shulgi is genrally considered the primogenator of the sorcerer caste. Although I suppose that's redundant since they can all do blood magic in v5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-10T23:57:06-08:00","id":1476194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1475813-player-s-guide-and-blood-sigils-for-vtm-announced?p=1476170#post1476170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supposedly something like 2/3 of all Assamite sorcerers are descended from him, most prominently Al-Ashrad.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't know that, but doesn't it also makes a loresheet for his descendants kind of pointless? It is like making the loresheet for Assamite Sorcerers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-11T20:05:22-08:00","id":1476250,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m looking forward to the Player\u2019s Guide, but I\u2019m nervous about Blood Sigil. Blood Sorcery is already the most bloated discipline, even AFTER it was pared down from V20. Easily one of the best parts of V5 is that Tremere are much more balanced than they used to be. I hope we aren\u2019t going to go back to the bad old days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26481-tiltowait","name":"tiltowait","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-11T20:14:03-08:00","id":1476251,"title":"","content":"At least the elimination of Paths means every published Tremere character doesn't have an extra 20+ dots in disciplines at their disposal. Rituals work a bit better both thematically and for game balance what with the time and preparation required.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-11T21:13:45-08:00","id":1476255,"title":"","content":"I don't think rituals were particularly problematic before, but don't have a problem with them now either. For Paths though, agreed, while I'm on the opinion that limiting a V5 Discipline to 1-power-per-level isn't the best design choice, making sorcerers, especially the Tremere, follow the same rules as everyone else is a major improvement.<br /> <br /> For now I think this is enough to deter the unavoidable sorcery bloat from becoming a serious problem.<br /> <br /> But I do miss the details in the distinct sorcery Disciplines that made them intrinsically linked to the culture of each magical group, even more than I miss the specific powers. Koldunism, Thaumaturgy and Dur-An-Ki aren't the same thing in lore and shouldn't feel the same even when they're doing the same things (they can still be mechanically equivalent, no problem).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-12T01:40:33-08:00","id":1476264,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I sort of feel like a better route would be generic Paths with paradigm-specific rider effects to represent the different schools of Blood Magic. This is sort of how Warhammer Fantasy Roleplay 4e does it, collapsing lots of disparate traditions into a much smaller list of spells. Then you wouldn't need Paths, Ways and Krainas that overlap or repeat themes; you'd just have one set of base rules with modifiers based on your paradigm.<br /> <br /> So, you may have a common list of weather manipulation, spirit manipulation, fire, telekinesis and blood manipulation, but the paradigm rider modifies them somewhat by requiring a certain sacrifice or focus (blood for Tremere, talismans or astrology for Banu Haqim, native soil for Tzimisce, infernal True Names for Baali, runes that cause self-inflicted damage for Lhiannon, and so on), or by adding specific effects.<br /> <br /> A Koldun with the base weather powers might add an effect unique to their connection to the land; Banu Haqim might manifest their powers as the intervention of djinn, creating obvious displays of the supernatural even for subtle spells; Lhiannon might be able to sustain a spell for as long as a rune remains on her skin but takes a level of lethal damage she cannot heal without removing the rune; Setites gain extra bonuses when manipulating desires and base passions, or perhaps faith; and so on.<br /> <br /> Then there may be a select number of unique rituals for each paradigm that are only available to those schools of magic, to fill in the gaps left behind by the reduced number of Paths.<br /> <br /> Because of time, though, I just implemented a simple house rule: in V20, Tremere can learn their primary Path as in-Clan, but all the others count as out-of-Clan. The only benefit is that because of the Clan structure, they can attempt to access those additional Paths through mentors and favours, although always at a cost. <br /> <br /> Furthermore, each paradigm has a limited list of Paths they can learn, with Thaumaturgy and Dur-An-Ki being the most flexible in terms of what's available (they get everything), but other Clans and Bloodlines only accessing a narrow range.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 03-12-2022, 05:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T15:16:17-07:00","id":1476466,"title":"","content":"I'm just pissed that Necromancy (sorry, Oblivion) gets the short straw again. I mean fine, we get a few new rituals for Blood Sorcery and some new stuff for thinbloods but what about Abyss Mysticism and Necromancy? The Cult of the Blood Gods gave a few new rituals but it's still a far cry from what we had previously. And they have never released a book fully dedicated to Necromancy, but Thaum has 3 books dedicated to it (with some Assamite, Setite and Tzimisce sorcery thrown in for good measure).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T16:15:29-07:00","id":1476470,"title":"","content":"Vampires should have the ability to control the weather. If they don't want it to be a Thaum path anymore, then make it something else. A Dominate fifth level power where you Dominate the weather. An Animalism fifth level power where you send your beast into the atmosphere creating a roaring thunderstorm. An Oblivion power where you pull part of the underworld's maelstrom into the living world. I don't care what you make it a part of, but weather control is a classic Dracula power and should exist in some form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T16:29:38-07:00","id":1476472,"title":"","content":"Any word on the player's guide possible release date?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T16:39:39-07:00","id":1476473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo